      en: "Thermo Fisher Scientific Vilnius is one of the world's leading competence centers for molecular biology and biotechnology. The site originates from the Institute of Enzymology founded in 1975, which later gained global recognition as 'Fermentas' before being acquired by Thermo Fisher Scientific in 2010. Today, over 1,500 highly skilled professionals work here, developing and manufacturing reagents, enzymes, and kits for life science research and diagnostics. During the COVID-19 pandemic, the plant played a critical role in producing components for PCR tests and mRNA vaccines. The Vilnius campus features state-of-the-art laboratories and cleanrooms certified to the highest international standards. The presence of this global giant has turned Vilnius into a biotechnology hotspot in Eastern Europe and fosters close cooperation with Vilnius University. The company continuously invests in expanding its capabilities to meet the growing worldwide demand for biotechnological solutions.",
